      "lineNbr": 4778,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-22T23:46:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why is this needed? If you have a ramdump, then you can look at devices_kset-\u003elist and see which dev is causing the hang-during-shutdown case you describe. This hook seems unnecessary.",
      "revId": "123ef0a2c5f4b62db9edec5b99d2203e2ea0644a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1c4f79b_efd3830e",
        "filename": "drivers/base/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4778,
      "author": {
        "id": 1982050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T01:01:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The device doing a shutdown is already deleted from the `devices_kset-\u003elist`, so it is not possible to determine which device is in the process of shutting down by looking at the `devices_kset-\u003elist`.\n\n```\n{\n\tdev \u003d list_entry(devices_kset-\u003elist.prev, struct device,\n\t\t\tkobj.entry);\n\t...\n\tlist_del_init(\u0026dev-\u003ekobj.entry);   //\u003c--------- deleted from the list\n\t...\n\t(call shutdown(dev))\n\t...\n}\n```\n\nAlthough we can find the corresponding device through the Ramdump analysis, it is a time-consuming task.\nAnd the Ramdump is not always completely delivered to us. There are often cases where some files are corrupted and cannot be analyzed.\n\nThe information stored in this vendor hook is included in the report generated by the bootloader, which we can quickly check.",
      "parentUuid": "a2731923_e9b7ea40",
      "revId": "123ef0a2c5f4b62db9edec5b99d2203e2ea0644a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e959205_e5c257aa",
        "filename": "drivers/base/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4778,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T08:54:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Passing in a \"raw\" device pointer is not going to provide you any real information as you have no context or knowledge of what that pointer really is.  This isn\u0027t going to give you any real information.",
      "parentUuid": "b1c4f79b_efd3830e",
      "revId": "123ef0a2c5f4b62db9edec5b99d2203e2ea0644a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
